STRINGTABLE
BEGIN
    IDS_WORKSTATION_TYPE    "\r\n  In this step, DeltaV Workstation Configuration will collect\n  information about the type of workstation you wish to install.\n  The types of workstations include ProfessionalPLUS, Professional,\n  Operator, Application, Base, and Inter-Zone Servers.  \r\n\r\n  If you purchased Simulate Standalone you will want to select the\n  Simulate option for standalone laptop or workstation. If you\n  purchased Simulate Multi-node, you should select the type of\n  Simulate Multi-Node workstation you are installing \n  (e.g., Professional Plus). Be sure to check the appropriate box\n  correctly - once you start the installation, the type  of workstation\n  is permanent.  \r\n\r\n  Select the type of workstation to install and press NEXT button. If\n  you are unsure, press the EXIT to exit without changing your\n  configuration."
    IDS_PROWORKSTATION      "\r\n   You have chosen to install a ProfessionalPLUS workstation.\n   Please verify the required information below and then press the\n   NEXT button."
    IDS_LANCARDASSIGNMENT   "\r\n   In this step, specify the network cards to assume the primary\n   and secondary network functions. The selected network card(s)\n   will be used to communicate with other DeltaV Stations on\n   the ACN."
    IDS_IPADDRESSASSIGNMENT "\r\n   In this step, DeltaV Workstation Configuration will collect IP and\n   subnet addressing information. Below, you need to fill in the\n   primary and secondary (if your network has redundant LAN's) IP,\n   direct link and subnet addresses. If you are installing an\n   Application or Operator workstation, your IP addresses are\n   automatically assigned and are shown here only for informational\n   purposes. Press the NEXT button after you have entered and/or\n   reviewed the required address information."
    IDS_INTGOPERWKSTN       "\r\n  You have chosen a workstation type that requires a configuration\n  file (CFG). Some workstation types can be local or remote\n  depending on the settings in the workstation CFG file. Click the\n  Browse button to select the CFG file containing the configuration\n  for the workstation you want to install. After DeltaV Workstation\n  Configuration lists the workstations in the CFG file, select one to\n  install, then click the Next button to continue."
    IDS_SHOWCONFIGURATION   "\r\n   Your DeltaV workstation is ready to be setup using the \r\n   parameters displayed below. You should verify these  \r\n   settings before pressing the NEXT button to ensure that \r\n   your DeltaV workstation is configured properly. After you \r\n   verify the configuration settings below, press the next \r\n   button to begin the installation."
    IDS_ENDPROGRAM          "\r\n   The first stage of the setup process has completed.          \r\n   You must restart your DeltaV workstation before the   \r\n   changes made can become effective.                                      \r\n   The installation process will continue after your computer \r\n   is restarted."
    IDS_PICK_A_WORKSTATION_TYPE 
                            "You must select which workstation type to install before continuing."
    IDS_NO_WKSTN_NAME       "You must enter the DeltaV System Name and Workstation Name before continuing."
    IDS_NO_NETWORK_TYPE     "You must choose network redundancy options before continuing."
    IDS_SERVER_TYPE         "\r\n   In this step, DeltaV Workstation Configuration will collect\n   information about your network environment.  To properly\n   configure your workstation, the wizard need to know if this\n   workstation is going to operate in workgroup or in a domain.                                      \r\n\r\n   The default network type and network name have been chosen\n   for you. Verify these settings or correct them and press the NEXT\n   button. If you are unsure of your network type or network name,\n   press the EXIT button to exit and contact your network\n   administrator for the required information."
    IDS_REGISTRY_MSG_ERROR  "An error occurred while setting up the Windows NT registry for HAWK services.\nSee your system administrator for an explanation of error : "
    IDS_SERVICE_UPDATE_ERROR "Error updating password for service: "
    IDS_WORKSTATION_TYPE2   "\r\n   This file is created by using the DeltaV Explorer          \r\n   function ""Create Station Configuration File""."
    IDS_INSTALL_WORKSTATION "\r\n   Your workstation is being configured to run DeltaV. The\n   configuration process is fully automatic. When the install has\n   completed, your machine will either be restarted or logged off,\n   depending on its initial state."
    IDS_CHOOSE_DVDATA_BACKUP 
                            "Choose the previous DeltaV\\DVData directory then click OK."
END

